From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - keep a padded SPU-M hash chunk within the payload limit

handle_ahash_req() cuts a hash request into chunks of at most
max_payload bytes, and on SPU-M appends the MD5/SHA padding to the last
chunk in software. max_payload is already the largest value the 16-bit
BD Payload Length field holds, rounded down to the block size, so the
padding can push the last chunk past it. A last chunk of 65464 to
65472 bytes (64-byte blocks) or 65392 to 65408 bytes (SHA-384/512)
becomes 65536 bytes, which the BD size and MAC length fields truncate
to 0. On BCM6755 the SPU never answers such a request and every later
one queues behind it, so a single AF_ALG digest of 65471 bytes through
md5-iproc wedges the engine; 65408 and 65463 bytes still work.

When the padded last chunk would not fit, send all but its last
partial or full block as an ordinary chunk and hash the rest, padded,
in the next one.

Fixes: 9d12ba86f818 ("crypto: brcm - Add Broadcom SPU driver")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
@@ -758,6 +758,13 @@ static int handle_ahash_req(struct iproc_reqctx_s *rctx)
 	    (chunksize > ctx->max_payload))
 		chunksize = ctx->max_payload;
 
+	if (rctx->is_final && (chunksize == nbytes_to_hash) &&
+	    (ctx->max_payload != SPU_MAX_PAYLOAD_INF) &&
+	    (chunksize + spu->spu_hash_pad_len(hash_parms.alg, hash_parms.mode,
+					       chunksize, blocksize) >
+	     ctx->max_payload))
+		chunksize = rounddown(chunksize - 1, blocksize);
+
 	/*
 	 * If this is not a final request and the request data is not a multiple
 	 * of a full block, then simply park the extra data and prefix it to the
